# Full textbook wording

When building IELTS course exercises from the coursebook / Teacher’s Book:

- Use the **complete** original sentences, questions, options, and instructions.
- Do **not** invent shortened labels like `Sentence 1 (…-library loan)`, ellipsis summaries, or paraphrased stubs “to save space”.
- If a later exercise refers to earlier sentences (e.g. 2b → 2a), show those **full** sentences again (filled forms OK when the book assumes they were completed).
- Fit layout by tightening padding/gaps/type size or using two columns — **never** by cutting the learner-facing text.
- Answer keys may be short; **stem / option / passage text must stay complete**.
